---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
import CallLink from '../components/ui/CallLink.astro';
import { site } from '../content/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Yanta"
  description="How Yanta collects, uses and stores the information you give us when you enquire about plant hire or poly welding."
>
  <Section>
    <div class="prose-yanta mx-auto max-w-[760px]">
      <h1 class="text-(length:--text-hero) leading-[1.1] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.5px] text-navy">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">
        Yanta ({site.owners}) operates this website. We're a family plant hire and civil business based near
        Rockhampton, Queensland, and we handle your information in line with the Australian Privacy Act 1988
        and the Australian Privacy Principles.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-(length:--text-section) font-extrabold text-navy">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        When you submit an enquiry form we collect what you type in: your name, phone number, email address,
        company (if given), the job location and the details of the machine or service you're asking about.
        We also record which page you enquired from and, if you arrived from an ad, basic campaign information
        (such as UTM tags or click identifiers) so we know which advertising works.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        Like most websites, we use analytics and advertising tags (Google Analytics, Google Ads and Meta Pixel)
        that collect standard usage data such as pages viewed and approximate location. These tools use cookies
        or similar identifiers. You can limit them with your browser settings or ad preferences on those platforms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-(length:--text-section) font-extrabold text-navy">Why we collect it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        One reason: to respond to your enquiry with a quote and organise the hire or job you asked about.
        Campaign information is used only to measure our own advertising. We don't sell your information,
        rent it out, or use it for anything unrelated to your enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-(length:--text-section) font-extrabold text-navy">Who handles it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        Form submissions are delivered to us by our form provider and arrive as email to our business inboxes.
        Analytics and advertising data is processed by Google and Meta under their own privacy policies.
        Beyond those service providers, your details stay with us.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-(length:--text-section) font-extrabold text-navy">Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        We keep enquiry details for as long as needed to handle the job and our business records, and no longer.
        If you'd like the information you've sent us corrected or deleted, contact us and we'll do it —
        email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="font-semibold text-navy underline">{site.email}</a> or
        ring <CallLink class="font-semibold text-navy underline" /> and ask.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-(length:--text-section) font-extrabold text-navy">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
        Questions or concerns about privacy: {site.owners}, Yanta —
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`} class="font-semibold text-navy underline">{site.email}</a>,
        <CallLink class="font-semibold text-navy underline" />. If you're not satisfied with our response,
        you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au).
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
